-- title:
--   Finite flat Hopf models over mathbb Z_{(ℓ)} exist
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and let $C$ be an arbitrary term of the structure `JZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore p q A hA` (fppf sheaves over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ together with flat finite-type $\mathbb Z$-Hopf algebras $H_m$ representing their sections, generic- and $A$-fibre parametrisations of the relevant torsion subgroups, short exact sequences and Kummer rows; these fields are summarised here). Then the type `JZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionFFModels p q A hA C` is nonempty: there exist, for every $m$ and every prime $\ell \neq p$, a commutative ring $H^{\mathrm{ff}}_{m,\ell}$ carrying a cocommutative Hopf-algebra structure over [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) (the subring of $\mathbb Q$ of fractions whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$), finite and flat as a module over it, and a bijection from the algebra homomorphisms $H^{\mathrm{ff}}_{m,\ell} \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ over that subring, with their convolution product, onto `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m` — the subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ killed by $q^m$ and contained in the supremum of the Hecke-torsion submodules for the powers of the Eisenstein maximal ideal — sending convolution to addition and commuting with the action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$; and, provided $q \neq p$, a finite cocommutative $\mathbb Z/q$-Hopf algebra $\bar H_m$ with a surjective ring homomorphism $H^{\mathrm{ff}}_{m,q} \to \bar H_m$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by $q$.
--
--   This is the existence statement for finite flat Hopf-algebra models over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$, $\ell \neq p$, of the $\mathfrak P$-primary $q^m$-torsion of $J_0(p)$, together with their reductions modulo $q$; it holds for every core, the models being obtained by base change from the $\mathbb Z$-Hopf algebras of the core. It is used by [`ModularCurve.hasJZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionSheaf_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.hasJZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionSheaf_of_dvd) and by [`ModularCurve.hasJZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_two_residue_iff_reductionModL_of_dvd_eisensteinNumerator_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.hasJZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_two_residue_iff_reductionModL_of_dvd_eisensteinNumerator_v5).
